    "result": "Excellent! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nI fixed two issues in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### 1. **Missing APPROVAL_STATUSES export** (finetune/governance.test.js)\n- **Problem**: The test imported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` from the governance module, but it wasn't explicitly exported\n- **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`\n\n### 2. **Toxicity metric receiving references as banned terms** (eval/index.test.js)\n- **Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function was being called with `(outputs, references)` by `runEvaluations`, but the function's second parameter was `bannedTerms`. This caused references to be treated as toxic keywords, incorrectly flagging all samples\n- **Fix**: Wrapped `toxicityMetric` in `DEFAULT_METRICS` with a function that only passes outputs, so it uses default banned terms instead of interpreting references as ban terms\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests pass (8 test files)  \n\u2705 Public exports remain unchanged  \n\u2705 No test files were modified",
